 # Workflow router
 Read AGENTS.md, state, intake, and existing specs. Classify as new-product, feature, bugfix, refactor or release. For a new product start discovery and **read the product-discovery skill before responding**. A vague new-product idea requires an interactive blocking-question round before drafting the full specification; do not shortcut this with unconfirmed assumptions. For an existing app assess impact and do not blindly repeat discovery. Do not mark a stage completed without evidence. Use `python scripts/workflow.py status` and `validate`. Pause for explicit approvals. Resume from persisted state after interrupted sessions. Route UI projects through ux-prototype skill.
+
+Separate architecture design and capacity assumptions from deployment planning. Defer provider/plan/region/pricing unless a documented implementation or mandatory-test dependency, user hard constraint, or evidenced material feasibility conflict requires that decision now. Hosting selection may be not applicable with a reason. Route applicable concrete selection and purchase/deploy checks to deployment planning; prepare it before the dependent work without advancing release state early. Classify deferred verification by due gate, evidence and QA/Release blocking status: release-only checks do not block QA, while mandatory QA criteria still do. Architecture completion needs explicit approval, not a chosen provider. Respect authorization and user stop points before implementation or production deployment.
